+// The 12 FAAL settings used to live here as global JSMSetting objects, registered
+// by a static initialiser. They are now created in initJsmSettings() (main.cpp)
+// like every other setting of the program: heap-allocated, handed to
+// SettingsManager, which owns them, with the command registered next to them.
+//
+// That removes two problems at once:
+//   * no settings are registered during static initialisation, so nothing runs
+//     before main() and there is no static-initialisation-order dependency;
+//   * the settings are heap objects, so the shared_ptr map deletes them normally
+//     instead of calling operator delete on static storage at exit
+//     (which corrupted the heap: STATUS_HEAP_CORRUPTION on shutdown).
+//
+// This file is kept only because CMakeLists.txt still lists it; nothing includes
+// it. Read initJsmSettings() in main.cpp for the current definitions.
